1
00:00:01,160 --> 00:00:05,704
When you said you like me,
you meant as a friend, right?

2
00:00:05,740 --> 00:00:06,640
What do you think?

3
00:00:06,641 --> 00:00:07,840
Did something good happen?

4
00:00:08,040 --> 00:00:08,840
Huh?

5
00:00:08,970 --> 00:00:11,070
Your hair is sticking up.

6
00:00:11,080 --> 00:00:13,910
Mayama, have you and Asamiya
gotten really close lately?

7
00:00:14,380 --> 00:00:15,380
Ah...

8
00:00:15,480 --> 00:00:17,200
It smells like Asamiya.

9
00:00:17,680 --> 00:00:19,580
Honestly,
what do you think of Asamiya?

10
00:00:19,650 --> 00:00:20,720
I don't know.

11
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:22,220
He's way out of my reach.

12
00:00:22,340 --> 00:00:25,460
If you feel like Asamiya is out of reach,
then try harder to get closer to him.

13
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:29,390
When Asamiya said he likes me,
he meant as a friend, right?

14
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:30,700
No way.

15
00:00:31,390 --> 00:00:32,706
I ended up taking it way too far.

16
00:00:32,730 --> 00:00:33,600
I'm sorry.

17
00:00:33,630 --> 00:00:35,830
We want to get along with you too.

18
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:36,930
Huh?

19
00:00:36,980 --> 00:00:38,176
Let's be the event coordinators together.

20
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:39,559
Event coordinators?

21
00:00:39,560 --> 00:00:40,920
That's a great idea.

22
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:42,500
You don't mind, do you?

23
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:46,940
Being the cultural festival coordinators...
We didn't force you into this, did we?

24
00:00:47,640 --> 00:00:49,440
When Asamiya said he likes me...

25
00:00:50,410 --> 00:00:53,020
He didn't mean it as a friend.

26
00:00:55,060 --> 00:01:00,260
Someone like me doesn't deserve him at all.

27
00:01:10,660 --> 00:01:12,630
A haunted house.

28
00:01:18,900 --> 00:01:22,800
So, our class's cultural
festival event will be...

29
00:01:24,360 --> 00:01:25,760
A haunted house!

30
00:01:25,840 --> 00:01:27,350
Let's have a round of applause.

31
00:01:41,860 --> 00:01:43,159
The votes were really close.

32
00:01:43,160 --> 00:01:44,160
Yeah.

33
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:46,570
Our butler cafe idea
wasn't bad either, right?

34
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:48,080
Yeah.

35
00:01:48,760 --> 00:01:50,010
Then again...

36
00:01:53,820 --> 00:01:56,080
Welcome home, my lady.

37
00:01:58,440 --> 00:02:00,450
I thought it would be a huge hit...

38
00:02:01,660 --> 00:02:03,660
But this result isn't bad either.

39
00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:05,990
After all, Asamiya doesn't
want to be in the spotlight.

40
00:02:06,860 --> 00:02:09,400
If Asamiya doesn't show his
face, the whole plan falls apart.

41
00:02:10,090 --> 00:02:13,020
But Mayama, you wanted to see
Asamiya in a butler outfit too, right?

42
00:02:13,060 --> 00:02:14,600
No, I...

43
00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:16,500
I voted for it.

44
00:02:17,080 --> 00:02:18,080
I'm sorry.

45
00:02:19,200 --> 00:02:21,140
If it's just for Mayama to see,
I wouldn't mind.

46
00:02:24,300 --> 00:02:27,540
I'll focus on working behind the
scenes for the haunted house too.

47
00:02:27,680 --> 00:02:28,680
All right, all right.

48
00:02:29,100 --> 00:02:32,180
Then, let's all go shopping
for costumes this weekend.

49
00:02:32,880 --> 00:02:35,519
Before then, let's figure out
what kind of monsters we should be.

50
00:02:35,520 --> 00:02:36,320
Sounds good.

51
00:02:36,520 --> 00:02:40,360
Oh, Mayama, you're in
charge of being a monster.

52
00:02:41,920 --> 00:02:42,920
I'll do my best.

53
00:02:44,740 --> 00:02:45,779
This is gonna be fun.

54
00:02:45,780 --> 00:02:47,200
What should we do?

55
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:36,500
"After Moving Seats, The Boy Behind Me Has A Crush On Me"
(Episode 3)

56
00:03:39,450 --> 00:03:40,980
How do I look?

57
00:03:42,660 --> 00:03:43,660
Looks good.

58
00:03:44,460 --> 00:03:45,460
Thanks.
You're a lifesaver.

59
00:03:47,600 --> 00:03:49,790
I can't believe you're
going shopping with friends.

60
00:03:49,960 --> 00:03:52,900
It's a bit far,
but I'm so glad you chose this school.

61
00:03:53,120 --> 00:03:54,680
We're just going shopping for supplies.

62
00:03:55,060 --> 00:03:58,000
But this is the first time
you've cared so much about your outfit.

63
00:03:59,300 --> 00:04:02,840
Could it be you have a crush on a girl?

64
00:04:06,010 --> 00:04:07,340
Just kidding.

65
00:04:07,610 --> 00:04:09,010
It's an all-boys school, after all.

66
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:11,080
Yeah.

67
00:04:13,080 --> 00:04:14,200
When you said you like me...

68
00:04:14,820 --> 00:04:18,720
When Asamiya said he likes me,
he meant as a friend, right?

69
00:04:19,090 --> 00:04:21,090
You probably say that to everyone else too.

70
00:04:23,230 --> 00:04:24,480
As if.

71
00:04:26,090 --> 00:04:27,090
Hare?

72
00:04:27,700 --> 00:04:29,419
We're really just shopping for supplies.

73
00:04:29,420 --> 00:04:30,420
That's not what I meant.

74
00:04:31,230 --> 00:04:32,570
Are you going to be on time?

75
00:04:32,600 --> 00:04:33,600
Huh?

76
00:04:34,020 --> 00:04:35,020
Oh, crap.

77
00:04:35,680 --> 00:04:36,680
I'm heading out!

78
00:04:36,840 --> 00:04:37,840
Be careful on the way!

79
00:04:57,760 --> 00:04:59,030
Made it.

80
00:05:07,200 --> 00:05:08,200
Mayama.

81
00:05:19,980 --> 00:05:21,779
Do I look weird?

82
00:05:21,780 --> 00:05:22,780
Ah.

83
00:05:23,440 --> 00:05:26,240
I just thought you give off a
totally different vibe in casual clothes.

84
00:05:26,860 --> 00:05:28,020
What's that supposed to mean?

85
00:05:29,930 --> 00:05:31,560
Where are Sakaki and Tsunekawada?

86
00:05:31,900 --> 00:05:35,400
They went ahead to buy props.
Sounds like it'll take a while.

87
00:05:36,340 --> 00:05:37,340
I see.

88
00:05:40,080 --> 00:05:41,800
I didn't expect you to dress so maturely.

89
00:05:42,640 --> 00:05:43,710
Does it look weird?

90
00:05:44,480 --> 00:05:45,910
The size isn't quite right either.

91
00:05:46,440 --> 00:05:47,720
These are my brother's clothes.

92
00:05:48,340 --> 00:05:49,310
Your dear brother.

93
00:05:49,311 --> 00:05:50,850
What do you mean, "dear brother"?

94
00:05:52,080 --> 00:05:55,150
I didn't know what to
wear for something like this.

95
00:05:59,250 --> 00:06:00,250
Huh?

96
00:06:02,590 --> 00:06:04,560
Let's roll up your cuffs a bit.

97
00:06:20,930 --> 00:06:25,050
And since the clothes are more mature...

98
00:06:31,130 --> 00:06:32,550
You could part your hair a little.

99
00:06:34,330 --> 00:06:35,330
Looks good.

100
00:06:38,630 --> 00:06:40,860
I guess clothes really do make the man.

101
00:06:42,030 --> 00:06:43,030
Not at all.

102
00:06:43,870 --> 00:06:44,870
Huh?

103
00:06:46,490 --> 00:06:49,370
Mayama, you don't give
yourself enough credit.

104
00:06:52,540 --> 00:06:53,829
Oh, sorry to keep you waiting.

105
00:06:53,830 --> 00:06:55,240
Sorry for the wait.

106
00:06:57,250 --> 00:06:58,250
No way.

107
00:06:58,850 --> 00:07:00,549
Asamiya actually isn't late.

108
00:07:00,550 --> 00:07:04,810
True. When he makes plans with us,
he's usually either late or flakes on us.

109
00:07:05,190 --> 00:07:06,190
Is that true?

110
00:07:06,620 --> 00:07:08,490
How could I ever make Mayama wait?

111
00:07:10,330 --> 00:07:13,000
The Mayama effect is seriously powerful.

112
00:07:13,910 --> 00:07:14,910
Let's go.

113
00:07:18,170 --> 00:07:19,770
Is that really Asamiya?

114
00:07:19,870 --> 00:07:20,870
It's a little scary.

115
00:07:22,930 --> 00:07:23,930
Wow.

116
00:07:24,470 --> 00:07:26,710
What's the plan for today?
Where to first?

117
00:07:27,080 --> 00:07:28,600
Whose costume should we look at first?

118
00:07:30,410 --> 00:07:31,610
The weather is pretty nice.

119
00:07:31,850 --> 00:07:32,850
It really is.

120
00:07:33,080 --> 00:07:34,580
What should we start with?

121
00:07:34,820 --> 00:07:37,520
Mayama's costume first, of course.

122
00:07:37,570 --> 00:07:38,990
Mayama, huh.

123
00:07:39,170 --> 00:07:41,690
Let's get Mayama sorted out first.

124
00:07:45,390 --> 00:07:45,960
It's a bit hard to choose.

125
00:07:45,961 --> 00:07:47,106
Are you guys always like this?

126
00:07:47,130 --> 00:07:51,429
Whenever Asamiya is around, we get
three times as much attention as usual.

127
00:07:51,430 --> 00:07:52,230
Aren't they looking at me?
Of course they aren't looking at you.

128
00:07:53,130 --> 00:07:54,130
Huh?

129
00:07:54,540 --> 00:07:55,500
I always thought they were looking at me.

130
00:07:55,501 --> 00:07:57,410
Everyone is obviously looking at Asamiya.

131
00:07:58,970 --> 00:07:59,970
Seriously?

132
00:08:00,450 --> 00:08:01,180
Wait, really?

133
00:08:01,181 --> 00:08:02,461
All right, all right, all right.

134
00:08:02,550 --> 00:08:05,380
Uh...

135
00:08:06,880 --> 00:08:08,820
So what's the deal with this...

136
00:08:09,250 --> 00:08:12,519
After a heated debate
between Tsunekawada and me...

137
00:08:12,520 --> 00:08:14,859
We decided you should be a werewolf.

138
00:08:14,860 --> 00:08:15,860
Yeah.

139
00:08:15,990 --> 00:08:16,990
Try it on.

140
00:08:25,490 --> 00:08:28,249
Something feels a bit off.

141
00:08:28,250 --> 00:08:30,840
It's not exactly scary.

142
00:08:32,070 --> 00:08:33,240
What do you think, Asamiya?

143
00:08:33,580 --> 00:08:34,580
It's cute.

144
00:08:36,410 --> 00:08:39,280
Shouldn't a werewolf be less cute?

145
00:08:41,020 --> 00:08:42,020
No.

146
00:08:42,420 --> 00:08:43,860
It's actually a great selling point.

147
00:08:43,920 --> 00:08:45,150
A cute werewolf.

148
00:08:45,990 --> 00:08:47,090
Playing against type, huh.

149
00:08:48,270 --> 00:08:50,060
I'll go find a costume that matches.

150
00:08:52,560 --> 00:08:54,930
Asamiya is super fired up.

151
00:08:55,030 --> 00:08:56,999
When we first asked him to be
the cultural festival coordinator...

152
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:58,570
He didn't seem interested at all.

153
00:08:58,600 --> 00:08:59,600
Yeah.

154
00:09:01,310 --> 00:09:04,739
All right, we'll leave Mayama to Asamiya.

155
00:09:04,740 --> 00:09:06,239
Let's go look for our own costumes.

156
00:09:06,240 --> 00:09:07,240
Yeah.

157
00:09:15,410 --> 00:09:16,650
Which one should we start with?

158
00:09:33,050 --> 00:09:34,100
Weird.

159
00:09:35,700 --> 00:09:36,740
What's wrong?

160
00:09:37,930 --> 00:09:38,930
This...

161
00:09:39,010 --> 00:09:40,810
I can't quite get this choker on.

162
00:09:42,170 --> 00:09:43,170
I see.

163
00:09:46,110 --> 00:09:47,110
Huh?

164
00:09:49,830 --> 00:09:51,220
Huh? Wait?

165
00:09:53,410 --> 00:09:54,410
Huh?

166
00:09:56,410 --> 00:09:57,410
Hold still.

167
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:08,000
All done.

168
00:10:08,630 --> 00:10:09,630
Thanks.

169
00:10:17,270 --> 00:10:18,270
Perfect.

170
00:10:21,150 --> 00:10:22,350
There you go, sir.

171
00:10:25,250 --> 00:10:26,260
Did I startle you?

172
00:10:46,580 --> 00:10:48,740
Sakaki and the others
said they'll be a while.

173
00:10:49,370 --> 00:10:50,370
I see.

174
00:10:51,190 --> 00:10:52,190
Let's sneak out.

175
00:10:52,470 --> 00:10:53,470
Huh?

176
00:10:55,130 --> 00:10:55,850
Come on.
Huh?

177
00:11:16,370 --> 00:11:18,510
Vanilla or swirl, which one do you want?

178
00:11:19,070 --> 00:11:20,840
You can have whichever you like, Asamiya.

179
00:11:22,080 --> 00:11:23,080
Then...

180
00:11:25,030 --> 00:11:26,030
Thanks.

181
00:11:32,750 --> 00:11:34,720
Is it really okay for us to just sneak off?

182
00:11:36,890 --> 00:11:37,890
Want a bite?

183
00:11:40,050 --> 00:11:41,600
Hurry, it's melting.

184
00:11:45,290 --> 00:11:46,290
Yeah.

185
00:11:53,930 --> 00:11:54,930
It's good.

186
00:11:55,440 --> 00:11:56,440
I'm glad.

187
00:12:11,630 --> 00:12:12,950
It looks like it's about to melt.

188
00:12:17,250 --> 00:12:18,250
Yeah...

189
00:12:27,250 --> 00:12:29,750
Is there anywhere you want to go later?

190
00:12:30,810 --> 00:12:32,050
Hmm...

191
00:12:32,680 --> 00:12:33,680
What about you, Asamiya?

192
00:12:35,850 --> 00:12:37,350
Wherever you want to go.

193
00:12:39,010 --> 00:12:42,660
That actually makes it harder to answer...

194
00:12:44,010 --> 00:12:45,010
Ah.

195
00:12:50,714 --> 00:12:52,461
[Vintage books]

196
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:16,120
A bookstore?

197
00:13:18,690 --> 00:13:20,900
It's a bit out of the
way to go after school.

198
00:13:23,810 --> 00:13:25,330
I didn't know you read.

199
00:13:25,670 --> 00:13:27,800
I read about one book a month.

200
00:13:30,370 --> 00:13:31,610
I never knew that.

201
00:13:33,110 --> 00:13:34,110
What about you, Asamiya?

202
00:13:34,690 --> 00:13:35,690
Do you read?

203
00:13:36,190 --> 00:13:39,050
I was just thinking if Mayama reads,
maybe I should start too.

204
00:13:39,680 --> 00:13:40,880
Oh...

205
00:13:45,520 --> 00:13:46,520
Tell me.

206
00:13:46,690 --> 00:13:47,990
What book do you recommend?

207
00:13:50,370 --> 00:13:51,370
Ah.

208
00:13:51,390 --> 00:13:52,760
Let me think.

209
00:13:53,300 --> 00:13:55,560
Then...

210
00:14:04,470 --> 00:14:05,470
Ah.

211
00:14:06,990 --> 00:14:08,240
How about this one?

212
00:14:12,050 --> 00:14:13,050
I'll take it.

213
00:14:15,250 --> 00:14:17,090
You should at least
read the synopsis first...

214
00:14:17,790 --> 00:14:18,790
I'll take this, please.

215
00:14:20,750 --> 00:14:22,260
That'll be 820 yen.

216
00:14:25,010 --> 00:14:26,010
Out of 1,000 yen.

217
00:14:27,900 --> 00:14:28,900
Mayama.

218
00:14:29,130 --> 00:14:30,130
Hmm?

219
00:14:33,200 --> 00:14:34,540
They said we can pick one.

220
00:14:36,510 --> 00:14:37,510
Oh.

221
00:14:38,440 --> 00:14:39,440
That's nice.

222
00:14:39,910 --> 00:14:41,210
There are four kinds in total.

223
00:14:43,050 --> 00:14:44,210
I'll take this one then.

224
00:14:44,410 --> 00:14:45,410
Okay.

225
00:14:48,210 --> 00:14:50,150
Here's 180 yen in change.

226
00:14:52,350 --> 00:14:53,490
And here's your item.

227
00:14:59,550 --> 00:15:00,550
Thank you.

228
00:15:02,460 --> 00:15:03,460
Here.

229
00:15:03,510 --> 00:15:04,510
Huh?

230
00:15:04,610 --> 00:15:05,610
A gift for you.

231
00:15:06,450 --> 00:15:08,896
It goes perfectly with your name, Hare.
[TN: His name is the character for sunny weather]

232
00:15:11,470 --> 00:15:12,470
Thanks.

233
00:15:14,410 --> 00:15:15,440
Wait a sec.

234
00:15:19,190 --> 00:15:20,380
Ah, sorry.

235
00:15:20,850 --> 00:15:21,980
My phone died just now.

236
00:15:23,650 --> 00:15:25,190
Yeah, got it.

237
00:15:28,830 --> 00:15:29,930
Sorry to keep you waiting.

238
00:15:30,330 --> 00:15:31,850
They said they just finished shopping.

239
00:15:31,990 --> 00:15:33,710
Looks like sneaking out was the right call.

240
00:15:34,060 --> 00:15:35,530
Sorry it took so long.

241
00:15:36,130 --> 00:15:38,146
It's been a while since I
last went to a bookstore.

242
00:15:38,170 --> 00:15:40,440
I just couldn't stop browsing.

243
00:15:40,690 --> 00:15:44,540
It's fine. Seeing you so happy
makes me happy too.

244
00:15:46,640 --> 00:15:47,640
Um...

245
00:15:49,590 --> 00:15:50,590
Here.

246
00:15:54,510 --> 00:15:55,680
This is a return gift.

247
00:15:57,250 --> 00:16:00,660
Asamiya's name means a shining star,
Kousei, right?

248
00:16:01,450 --> 00:16:02,450
So...

249
00:16:11,300 --> 00:16:14,800
Our first bookstore date,
plus a gift from Mayama.

250
00:16:15,910 --> 00:16:17,739
Even if my life ended today,
I'd have no regrets.

251
00:16:17,740 --> 00:16:19,680
Don't say something so ominous.

252
00:16:21,030 --> 00:16:22,810
You didn't deny that it's a date.

253
00:16:22,910 --> 00:16:23,910
Huh?

254
00:16:24,050 --> 00:16:27,579
No, it's just that there were
too many things to point out.

255
00:16:27,580 --> 00:16:29,580
I just missed that one.

256
00:16:31,350 --> 00:16:33,690
Yeah, let's just go with that.

257
00:16:38,290 --> 00:16:39,330
Thank you.

258
00:16:41,110 --> 00:16:44,470
I should be thanking you.
I had a lot of fun today.

259
00:16:45,870 --> 00:16:47,070
What are you doing after this?

260
00:16:47,240 --> 00:16:49,770
Ah, I have to go home and do my homework.

261
00:16:50,530 --> 00:16:51,270
Makes sense.
What about you, Asamiya?

262
00:16:53,270 --> 00:16:54,350
I'm already done with mine.

263
00:16:54,640 --> 00:16:55,909
Just as expected of you.

264
00:16:55,910 --> 00:16:56,980
It's not because of that.

265
00:16:57,750 --> 00:16:59,870
It's because I wanted to keep
my whole day free today.

266
00:17:01,990 --> 00:17:02,990
Kousei?

267
00:17:04,850 --> 00:17:06,230
Long time no see.

268
00:17:06,560 --> 00:17:08,620
Did you get even more handsome?

269
00:17:09,110 --> 00:17:10,110
What are you doing here?

270
00:17:10,240 --> 00:17:11,760
Shopping. Just looking around.

271
00:17:13,260 --> 00:17:14,260
Who's this?

272
00:17:15,030 --> 00:17:16,230
A high school friend.

273
00:17:18,270 --> 00:17:19,470
Oh~.

274
00:17:25,440 --> 00:17:26,780
A middle school classmate.

275
00:17:42,690 --> 00:17:43,850
Thank you.

276
00:17:43,870 --> 00:17:45,090
For walking me home.

277
00:17:48,690 --> 00:17:50,200
So this is your house, Mayama.

278
00:17:51,270 --> 00:17:53,190
I'll come pick you up
every morning from now on.

279
00:17:53,800 --> 00:17:56,100
No need for that...

280
00:17:56,290 --> 00:17:57,290
Can't I?

281
00:17:58,610 --> 00:17:59,610
Yeah.

282
00:17:59,940 --> 00:18:01,010
You can't.

283
00:18:05,410 --> 00:18:06,620
I mean.

284
00:18:07,680 --> 00:18:08,979
Asamiya and I...

285
00:18:08,980 --> 00:18:11,020
Hare, you're back.

286
00:18:11,530 --> 00:18:12,530
Big brother.

287
00:18:12,590 --> 00:18:13,590
His older brother...

288
00:18:13,660 --> 00:18:14,660
Huh?

289
00:18:15,330 --> 00:18:19,330
Are you the friend he said
he was going shopping with today?

290
00:18:21,270 --> 00:18:22,270
Nice to meet you.

291
00:18:22,430 --> 00:18:23,530
I'm Asamiya Kousei.

292
00:18:24,300 --> 00:18:26,540
I'm Hare's older brother, Mayama Ten.

293
00:18:27,050 --> 00:18:30,669
Oh my, I'm so glad
Hare actually brought a friend home.

294
00:18:30,670 --> 00:18:31,809
Is that rare?

295
00:18:31,810 --> 00:18:34,240
Yeah, I'd say it's the first time.

296
00:18:35,230 --> 00:18:37,149
Would you like to come in
for a bit if you don't mind?

297
00:18:37,150 --> 00:18:38,880
He was just walking me home.

298
00:18:39,280 --> 00:18:40,710
Walking you home?

299
00:18:40,980 --> 00:18:41,980
Walking Hare home?

300
00:18:43,020 --> 00:18:44,150
Ah, well...

301
00:18:44,450 --> 00:18:45,450
Um...

302
00:18:45,750 --> 00:18:46,920
It's weird, right?

303
00:18:47,430 --> 00:18:50,160
Two guys going out of their
way to walk each other home.

304
00:18:51,030 --> 00:18:54,699
Mayama is just so cute,
I was worried someone might hit on him.

305
00:18:54,700 --> 00:18:56,729
Asamiya, what are you...

306
00:18:56,730 --> 00:18:58,029
I get it.

307
00:18:58,030 --> 00:18:58,730
Huh?

308
00:18:58,731 --> 00:19:02,070
Even though he's my little
brother, I think he's super cute too.

309
00:19:02,130 --> 00:19:05,240
But lately he's been distancing
himself from me. He's been so cold.

310
00:19:05,440 --> 00:19:06,230
Is that so?

311
00:19:06,231 --> 00:19:07,380
It sure is.

312
00:19:07,670 --> 00:19:11,179
The other morning he had bedhead and
said he was just going to school like that.

313
00:19:11,180 --> 00:19:13,050
I offered to fix it for him,
but he refused.

314
00:19:13,180 --> 00:19:14,780
- So cute.
- Right?

315
00:19:14,950 --> 00:19:18,250
Ah, by the way,
can we exchange contacts?

316
00:19:19,190 --> 00:19:20,220
Sure.

317
00:19:25,390 --> 00:19:27,200
What a beautiful sight.

318
00:19:27,670 --> 00:19:28,899
These two.

319
00:19:28,900 --> 00:19:29,900
All done.

320
00:19:31,510 --> 00:19:33,900
Oh shoot, I have to go to work.

321
00:19:34,240 --> 00:19:35,740
See you next time, Asamiya-kun.

322
00:19:35,970 --> 00:19:38,040
Okay, thank you.

323
00:19:44,110 --> 00:19:45,280
Your brother is really nice.

324
00:19:46,250 --> 00:19:48,050
Though he doesn't look
much like you, Mayama.

325
00:19:52,720 --> 00:19:55,560
We really don't, right?

326
00:19:56,790 --> 00:19:57,790
Huh?

327
00:20:00,360 --> 00:20:02,500
My brother is so handsome.

328
00:20:04,190 --> 00:20:09,640
He's tall, popular, and can do anything.

329
00:20:11,610 --> 00:20:12,980
But I'm...

330
00:20:23,490 --> 00:20:26,050
His brother really is outstanding.

331
00:20:26,370 --> 00:20:27,810
Not just handsome.

332
00:20:27,820 --> 00:20:30,090
He's smart and athletic too.

333
00:20:30,170 --> 00:20:32,590
- Yeah.
- But he's...

334
00:20:38,230 --> 00:20:39,230
Mayama?

335
00:20:40,490 --> 00:20:42,440
Sorry, it's nothing.

336
00:20:44,770 --> 00:20:46,240
How could it be nothing?

337
00:20:53,790 --> 00:20:55,650
When Asamiya confessed to me,

338
00:20:57,320 --> 00:21:00,290
I think I was actually really happy.

339
00:21:03,760 --> 00:21:05,430
Asamiya is very gentle.

340
00:21:05,950 --> 00:21:07,360
Being with you is really fun too.

341
00:21:08,910 --> 00:21:10,370
None of that is a lie.

342
00:21:12,630 --> 00:21:13,670
But...

343
00:21:17,640 --> 00:21:21,810
You can definitely find someone better.

344
00:21:25,080 --> 00:21:28,720
I fell for you
because you're Mayama.

345
00:21:30,390 --> 00:21:31,420
Why?

346
00:21:35,190 --> 00:21:38,660
I'm so plain.

347
00:21:39,600 --> 00:21:41,000
I don't stand out at all.

348
00:21:43,870 --> 00:21:45,670
So why would you...

349
00:21:49,090 --> 00:21:50,570
Because you're Mayama.

350
00:21:57,530 --> 00:21:59,250
That doesn't answer my question at all.

351
00:22:12,110 --> 00:22:15,330
Why do I like him so much?

352
00:22:25,910 --> 00:22:26,910
Um...

353
00:22:27,790 --> 00:22:29,326
If you don't mind, here's this for you.

354
00:22:29,350 --> 00:22:30,350
Is that okay?

355
00:22:30,610 --> 00:22:31,350
Yeah.
Thank you.

356
00:22:32,351 --> 00:22:33,680
- Take it with you.
- Okay.

357
00:22:35,530 --> 00:22:36,729
I'll wait for you again.

358
00:22:36,730 --> 00:22:37,730
Okay.

359
00:22:41,070 --> 00:22:43,090
Only one thing is for sure.

360
00:22:46,500 --> 00:22:48,830
Mayama is my first love.

361
00:24:12,750 --> 00:24:16,419
(Next Episode Preview) I don't know
how to act around Asamiya anymore.

362
00:24:16,420 --> 00:24:20,589
This is the first time we've all
prepared for something together so lively.

363
00:24:20,590 --> 00:24:22,389
So I want to make the
cultural festival a huge success.

364
00:24:22,390 --> 00:24:24,660
I've always watched Mayama from afar.

365
00:24:25,210 --> 00:24:29,560
It didn't take long for me
to realize these feelings were "love."

366
00:24:29,800 --> 00:24:30,970
Why do you want to date me?

367
00:24:30,980 --> 00:24:32,829
I saw the video. Can I
take a picture with you?

368
00:24:32,830 --> 00:24:34,170
That's so mean.

369
00:24:34,340 --> 00:24:37,209
My life has always been judged by my looks.

370
00:24:37,210 --> 00:24:38,539
You posted me on social media.

371
00:24:38,540 --> 00:24:40,169
Was it just to satisfy
your need for validation?

372
00:24:40,170 --> 00:24:42,339
You only have a pretty face.
Aren't you getting a little carried away?

373
00:24:42,340 --> 00:24:45,589
If I take a picture of Asamiya in drag,
my account will probably blow up too.

374
00:24:45,590 --> 00:24:48,020
Asamiya probably wouldn't
be too happy about that.

375
00:24:48,050 --> 00:24:50,069
Aren't Asamiya's feelings more important?

376
00:24:50,070 --> 00:24:51,070
I'm sorry.

377
00:24:51,420 --> 00:24:56,890
I never considered Mayama's feelings
and irresponsibly kept saying I liked him.
